attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a long spine.** Columns 0 to 24, `fadA` to `rarD`, are carried by 98 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0 to 27% of calls {S1}. The model names 34 to 100% of them, fewest at column 20, `rhtC`, 34% {S1}.

@variable **A fork follows at `yigG`**, column 25, carried by 67%, with an allophanate hydrolase-related protein at 25% {S2.c25}. Then the spine of columns 27 to 41, `corA` to `hemY`, [[uroporphyrinogen-III synthesis]], carried by 93 to 99% {S3, Q}. The last stretch, columns 61 to 79, `gppA` to `rbsK`, is variable, carried by 32 to 88%, [[branched-chain amino acid synthesis]] {S6.c64-79, Q}.

@model **The model names about as many genes on the spine columns as on the fork and variable ones**, 94 against 96%, and hesitates less there, 0.16 against 0.21 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 25, `yigG`, a fork column, 0.70 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on persistent families.** Columns 64 to 79, `ilvC` to `rbsK`, are carried from 82 to 32% of chromosomes {S6.c64-79}. The last column is `rbsK`, in 32% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 95% of genes**, 0.17 bits on average, perplexity 1.2 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.49 against 0.15 bits, and names fewer genes, 85% against 96% {C}.

